// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/referral_credit.t27 -- what an invited friend's rental earns the inviter
; This contract owns the referral credit the owner decided on 2026-09-26 (R3): the rate, the
; rounding, the base it is taken on, who is creditable, the holds a customer may place on it, how
; a hold is settled or paid out by hand, and the structure of the THB ledger that records every
; movement. It owns no edge, no code and no status of the referral graph: turbobaby/referral-program
; owns those and supplies the edge this credit is read from. It owns no order money: the order's
; total, its PromptPay amount and its deposit are turbobaby/order-money's, turbobaby/commerce's and
; turbobaby/deposit-tiers', and this file records only that the credit touches none of them.
; --
; THE OWNER'S WORDS, 2026-09-26, in translation (the Russian is verbatim in DECISIONS.md, "R1-R3,
; the owner's answers of 2026-09-26", and in src/trios/referral_credit.rs): "it must be credited
; only for someone who rented, a 10% discount"; "the inviter can take it as a discount on a rental
; or as money"; of the referral bonus points, "remove them, only the 10% discount"; and he
; confirmed the rule: when an invited friend completes a rental, the inviter is credited 10% of
; that rental's amount, excluding the deposit and delivery, "for each rental of the friend"; the
; inviter may spend it on their own rental or ask for a payout, which a manager makes by hand; the
; friend gets nothing. Asked the same day whether the 10% is taken before or after the referral
; balance the friend applied to that rental, he answered "after the discount -- 250" (the net base
; as built; OWNER_BASE_ANSWER_* below).
; --
; WHY A LEDGER OF ITS OWN (measured 2026-09-26 at e39221e). Three facts decide it.
; 1. THE SERVER NEVER KNOWS A RENTAL'S AMOUNT. check_full_subtotal in src/api/orders.rs prices a
;    bike line at 0 (D11), so a bike-only order stores subtotal = total = 0, and
;    BikeDeal::BikeRental's rate_thb_day is optional and never multiplied. So the 10% base can
;    only be a figure a manager records: BASE_IS_RECORDED_BY_A_MANAGER.
; 2. NO SHIPPED CLIENT CREATES A RENTAL ORDER: the cart kinds are the old catalogue's, book_block
;    answers NotWired, and turbobaby/order-presentation's CHECKOUT_BIKE_LINE_KEY_COUNT is 0. So a
;    hook in order completion would have nothing to compute, and the credit is born only when a
;    manager records a completed rental (POST /api/admin/referral-credit/rentals).
; 3. LOYALTY POINTS CANNOT PAY A RENTAL: bonus_used is bounded by a subtotal of 0, and a payout
;    from the points balance would pay out cashback. So the credit is a THB ledger apart from the
;    points (migration 089), whose balance is the sum of its rows and is stored nowhere, so it
;    cannot drift -- the defect turbobaby/loyalty-ledger measures in the points balance.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It restates no edge rule: the self edge, first touch and the
; confirmation are turbobaby/referral-program's, and the credit's own refusals (a self edge, an
; edge newer than the order, a customer from before the edge) are declared here as refusals of a
; CREDIT, not of an edge. It restates no identity proof: turbobaby/request-identity owns the
; gates, and this file counts which of its six routes stands behind which. It restates no notice:
; the admins' notice of a new request is operator-facing text, and turbobaby/notification-queue's
; queue carries none of it. It declares no customer sentence beyond the five the operator worded
; on 2026-09-26, and lists the eight it would have needed. No account id, no handle and no amount
; of any real person appears. It is ASCII; the owner's Russian is quoted where the code lives.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-referral-credit;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/referral-credit";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby referral credit: 10% of an invited friend's rentals, in THB";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-26";

; Where each rule below is implemented. The core is compiled for the host and for wasm32, so the
; server, the admin screen and the customer page run one arithmetic (D15).
pub const IMPLEMENTATION_CORE : str = "src/trios/referral_credit.rs";
pub const IMPLEMENTATION_DB : str = "src/db/referral_credit.rs";
pub const IMPLEMENTATION_API : str = "src/api/referral_credit.rs";
pub const MIGRATION : str = "migrations/089_referral_credit.sql";
pub const REGRESSION_WITNESS : str = "tests/integration_referral_credit.rs";
pub const WIRING_WITNESS : str = "tests/referral_credit_wiring.rs";

