; The recorder guard reads both identities check_admin answers with (the review of 2026-09-26;
; until then it ran only for an admin named by Telegram, so a password record of an admin's own
; friend credited that admin). check_admin answers the recorder's own id when Telegram names him,
; and 0 for the shared password token, a principal that names nobody (turbobaby/request-identity,
; PASSWORD_STEP_PRINCIPAL_IS_A_SENTINEL); initData that fails the strict check beside the token is
; answered with 0 as well. A named recorder is refused when he is the inviter. A password record is
; refused when the inviter is on ADMIN_IDS, since any listed admin may be the one holding the
; password. Both are 422 recorder_is_inviter and write nothing (recorder_refused below).
; STILL OPEN: a person who knows the password and is not on ADMIN_IDS can record the rentals of a
; friend he invited, and his record stores recorded_by = 0, which names nobody. The code cannot
; tell him from a manager; closing it means refusing the password token on this route, which would
; also refuse an admin whose WebView fails the strict check. That is the owner's call (DECISIONS.md).
pub const RECORDER_GUARD_REFUSES_A_NAMED_INVITER : bool = true;
pub const RECORDER_GUARD_REFUSES_A_PASSWORD_RECORD_OF_A_LISTED_ADMINS_FRIEND : bool = true;
