; The API's one shape. Both lanes compile against the wire types of IMPLEMENTATION_CORE, so a field
; cannot drift between the server and the Mini App. The path, the verb, the type a route answers
; with and the type a screen parses, the body a screen sends and the field names the server's
; hand-written parsers read are strings and choices, and no compiler compares them. Since the
; integration, API_SHAPE_WITNESS reads both sides against one table of the six routes, and the
; in-crate test named by API_SHAPE_BODY_WITNESS runs each shared body, serialized as a screen
; serializes it, through the server's parser. Eight planted drifts (a client path, a parsed type, a
; verb on each side, a field name, an answer type, a resolve action, a swapped body) each turned
; the witness red; tests/ui_endpoints_exist.rs, which only asks that a fetched path is served, went
; green with the merge.
pub const API_SHAPE_WITNESS : str = "tests/referral_credit_api_shape_wiring.rs";
pub const API_SHAPE_BODY_WITNESS : str = "src/api/referral_credit.rs the_bodies_the_screens_serialize_are_what_the_parsers_read";
